  "title": "The United States Congress should establish a National AI...",
  "created_at": "2026-08-11T13:17:05.846Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-08-11T13:17:12.121Z",
  "app_version": "v0.13.9-449-ge85c6a5d",
  "audience": "general_public",
  "phase": "opening",
  "topic": {
    "original": "The United States Congress should establish a National AI Injury Compensation\nProgram (NAIICP), modeled on the National Vaccine Injury Compensation Program (VICP), to\ngrant limited liability immunity to AI developers in exchange for a mandatory excise tax and\nadherence to tiered federal safety standards.",
    "refined": null,
    "final": "The United States Congress should establish a National AI Injury Compensation\nProgram (NAIICP), modeled on the National Vaccine Injury Compensation Program (VICP), to\ngrant limited liability immunity to AI developers in exchange for a mandatory excise tax and\nadherence to tiered federal safety standards.",
    "background": "The Logical Framework: The Noise Thesis:\nGround the affirmative case for maximizing the rate of AI development and adoption in the\nwork of Kahneman, Sibony, and Sunstein. Professional human judgment is inherently \"noisy\"\n(unwanted variability); auditable AI reduces this noise and improves accuracy to decrease\nharm. The Liability Chill: Current unlimited liability and the power disparity between tech\ngiants and individuals throttle the deployment of beneficial AI. The Mechanism: An excise tax\non AI services, tiered by risk (e.g., healthcare vs. social media) and safety compliance levels\n(basic safety vs state of the art safety practices), funds AI safety research, auditing, and a nofault administrative compensation board. Companies that do not adhere to safety standards\nare not covered and are not protected from unlimited liability. Compliance must be verified\nby hardware-level telemetry and cryptographically verifiable audit trails, overseen by an\nindependent, multi-disciplinary administrative board armed with federal subpoena power",
    "critique": {
